        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_22761e564f074295b6d235fc0410b695",
      "statement": "The QuickJS REPL provides capability-based isolation rather than OS isolation: the context has no ambient capabilities (no filesystem, network, fetch, require, process, or wall-clock time) with capabilities added only via programmatic tool calling, and execution is bounded by a per-call wall-clock timeout (default 5 s), a runtime-wide memory limit (default 64 MiB), and a per-call PTC host-call budget (default 256).",
